# IA Developer Tools — Mandatory Reference (ia-dev-workflow skill)

The skill at `~/.cursor/skills/ia-dev-workflow/SKILL.md` is the operational playbook for
setting up and driving the live IA environment (integrator.io staging + local connector
server + NetSuite/Shopify backend).

## When you MUST read it first

Read the skill BEFORE attempting any of these — do not improvise environment setup:

- **Reproducing a reported issue/bug** in this connector (or any IA epic) that requires a
  running environment, a flow run, or backend record inspection.
- **Verifying changes made by an epic** — after code/config/schema/hook changes, when you
  need to prove behavior end-to-end (run flow → inspect backend → assert).
- Any task mentioning: run the flow, ngrok/tunnel, persistSettings, reinstall the add-on,
  SuiteQL, platform script, rebuild the closure/bundle, fresh tile install, or
  "script execution time exceeded" / "invalid hook function" errors.

Follow the skill's steps in order (triple health check first). If a symptom matches a
documented failure signature, apply the documented fix before inventing a new diagnosis.

## Live-skill contract (MANDATORY after every session)

The skill is a living document. At the end of any repro/verification session, ask:
**"Did I hit a situation the skill did not cover, or where the skill was wrong/stale?"**

If yes, you MUST update the skill in the same session:

- **New failure signature + cause** → add a row to `troubleshooting.md` § "Failure
  signature → cause", and a technique write-up if the diagnosis was non-obvious.
- **New/changed command, API shape, or install step** → add/update the numbered section in
  `reference.md`; keep commands copy-pasteable with `$BASE`/`$TOK`-style variables.
- **New workflow stage or platform behavior** → extend the relevant Step in `SKILL.md`
  (keep SKILL.md a compact decision layer; push detail into the two sub-docs and link it).
- Never write tokens, account IDs, customer data, or any credential into skill files —
  reference `.env` keys instead.

Do not silently carry the learning only in the chat: if it isn't written into the skill,
it is lost. Tell the user what you added and where.
